{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome\/BeatUnitTied\/beatUnit"},"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"beatUnit"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL16MXLNoteKindValueO","text":"MXLNoteKindValue","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNoteKindValue"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"content":[{"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","text":"Discussion","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Maps to a nested MusicXML ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"<beat-unit>"},{"type":"text","text":" element."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Instance Property","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"externalID":"s:7IvorMXL12MXLMetronomeV12BeatUnitTiedV04beatE0AA16MXLNoteKindValueOvp","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"beatUnit","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLNoteKindValue","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL16MXLNoteKindValueO"}],"symbolKind":"property","title":"beatUnit"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome\/BeatUnitTied"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The beat-unit element indicates the graphical note type to use in a metronome mark."}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlmetronome\/beatunittied\/beatunit"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLMetronome":{"abstract":[{"text":"The metronome type represents metronome marks and other metric relationships. The beat-unit group and per-","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"minute element specify regular metronome marks. The metronome-note and metronome-relation elements allow for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the specification of metric modulations and other metric relationships, such as swing tempo marks where two","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"eighths are equated to a quarter note \/ eighth note triplet. Tied notes can be represented in both types of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"metronome marks by using the beat-unit-tied and metronome-tied elements. The parentheses attribute indicates","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"whether or not to put the metronome mark in parentheses; its value is no if not specified. The print-object","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"attribute is set to no in cases where the metronome element represents a relationship or range that is not","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"displayed in the music notation.","type":"text"}],"title":"MXLMetronome","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLMetronome"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLMetronome"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlmetronome","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLMetronome/BeatUnitTied/beatUnit":{"title":"beatUnit","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlmetronome\/beatunittied\/beatunit","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"The beat-unit element indicates the graphical note type to use in a metronome mark.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"beatUnit","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL16MXLNoteKindValueO","text":"MXLNoteKindValue","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome\/BeatUnitTied\/beatUnit"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"title":"IvorMXL","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","type":"topic","role":"collection"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLMetronome/BeatUnitTied":{"abstract":[{"text":"The beat-unit-tied type indicates a beat-unit within a metronome mark that is tied to the preceding beat-unit.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"This allows two or more tied notes to be associated with a per-minute value in a metronome mark, whereas the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"metronome-tied element is restricted to metric relationship marks.","type":"text"}],"title":"MXLMetronome.BeatUnitTied","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"BeatUnitTied","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"BeatUnitTied","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlmetronome\/beatunittied","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome\/BeatUnitTied"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNoteKindValue":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLNoteKindValue","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The note-type-value type is used for the MusicXML type element and represents the graphic note type, from","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"1024th (shortest) to maxima (longest).","type":"text"}],"title":"MXLNoteKindValue","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNoteKindValue","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnotekindvalue","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLNoteKindValue","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol"}}}